1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
"Paid for by..." Political ad names, decoded.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
The name tells you who paid. Not who paid them.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,400
Paid for by: Ohio Flyer PAC

4
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,200
Sounds like: A Dayton air show.

5
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,800
Actually: A super PAC set up to back Jon Husted. Its top donor ($1M) is a dark-money group that doesn’t disclose its own donors.

6
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:12,200
Paid for by: WinSenate

7
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,000
Sounds like: A game show.

8
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,600
Actually: Backs Sherrod Brown. An arm of Senate Majority PAC; its biggest funder is Majority Forward, a dark-money group.

9
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,000
Paid for by: No Going Back PAC

10
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,800
Sounds like: A breakup song.

11
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,400
Actually: Spent $20M+ against Brown. Its filings listed no donors as of mid-October; the NYT and Reuters report it’s funded by Trump’s super PAC, MAGA Inc.

12
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:25,800
Paid for by: Buckeye Freedom PAC

13
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,600
Sounds like: A tailgate.

14
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:31,200
Actually: Spent about $1.6M attacking Husted and promoting the Libertarian candidate. Donors disclosed so far: none.

15
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:32,600
Paid for by: Enough Promises Ohio

16
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,400
Sounds like: A progressive grassroots group.

17
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:38,000
Actually: Its mailers attack Brown and promote an independent. Its only donor Oct. 1–14: a Republican super PAC ($2.5M). The independent says he has no ties to it.

18
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,400
Ads are built to persuade. The record is built to check. We check every side: knowyourballot.netlify.app. Ohio votes Nov. 3.
